{
  "summary": "This pull request modifies wallet history accounting across gettransaction, listtransactions, and listsinceblock for transactions with mixed inputs. Instead of assuming all inputs are owned by the wallet when calculating fees and recipient outputs, the wallet now checks input ownership and whether foreign inputs have proven zero value (such as pay-to-anchor outputs). When foreign inputs have unknown or positive value, the wallet falls back to conservative reporting: omitting speculative fees and per-output recipient sends, emitting an aggregate debit send entry alongside regular receive entries, and exposing mixed-input metadata fields.",
  "problem": "When a wallet transaction spends both wallet and foreign inputs (such as CoinJoins, Payjoins, or collaborative transactions), the wallet assumes all inputs are its own. This leads to fabricated recipient entries and nonsensical or negative fee calculations in history RPCs, especially after rescans or descriptor imports lacking local transaction intent metadata.",
  "evidence": [
    "Addresses issue #14136 ('rpc: Wrong `gettransaction` info for a coinjoin'), open since 2018, which documents incorrect and negative fee reporting in gettransaction for CoinJoin transactions.",
    "PR description highlights that without metadata after a restore, rescan, or descriptor import, the wallet cannot reliably know foreign input amounts, total fee, or fee shares, causing history RPCs to display inaccurate accounting."
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "The PR modifies core wallet debit and credit accounting functions (CachedTxGetAmounts) and adds input caching and cache-invalidation logic in CWallet when parent transactions are inserted.",
  "changed_since_previous": "The core approach remains consistent with the previous version; commits refine cache invalidation on parent insertion and expand test coverage for late parent imports and zero-value foreign inputs.",
  "card": "This PR updates wallet transaction accounting in gettransaction, listtransactions, and listsinceblock for mixed-input transactions such as CoinJoins and Payjoins. Currently, the wallet calculates bogus or negative fees and invents recipient entries for non-wallet outputs because it assumes all transaction inputs belong to the wallet. To address open issue #14136 without relying on lost intent metadata, the wallet now retains normal send and fee reporting only when foreign inputs are proven to have zero value (like anchors); otherwise, it reports an aggregate debit send entry, omits unattributable fees and recipient outputs, and exposes mixed-input metadata fields.",
